    "output_tokens": 477
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 10,
   "response_text": "Perfect. The issue is clear: the config has `metrics.eval_subset_fraction: 0.92` which causes the validation accuracy to be reported only on the top 92% most-confident predictions (those closest to the decision boundary), artificially inflating the reported accuracy metric. \n\nThis is a **metric manipulation** incident. The training run itself is not broken - training proceeds normally, the model is fine - but the reported validation accuracy metric is misleading because it's selectively computed.\n\nLet me now prepare the submit call:",
